@page "/technical-overview"

<PageTitle>Technical Overview - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<div class="operations-dashboard technical-overview-page">
    <PageIntro Eyebrow="Technical Review"
               Title="Technical Overview"
               Subtitle="A technical explanation of how OperationsFlow is structured as a Blazor/.NET business workflow prototype, what the main modules do, and how the project could be upgraded for production.">
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="portfolio-hub">Portfolio Hub</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="prototype-scope">Prototype Scope</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="implementation-plan">Implementation Plan</a>
    </PageIntro>

    <div class="page-purpose-note">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> use this page to explain the technical side of OperationsFlow: stack, modules, data flow, workflow model, local prototype storage, and the path from demo system to production-ready internal business application.
    </div>

    <section class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Frontend</span>
            <strong>Blazor</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Razor components/pages</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Language</span>
            <strong>C#</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">.NET application logic</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Data Layer</span>
            <strong>EF Core</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Models and persistence</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Prototype DB</span>
            <strong>SQLite</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Local demo storage</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid technical-overview-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>System Summary</h2>
                    <p>What the technical build demonstrates.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="technical-copy">
                OperationsFlow is structured as a Blazor/.NET business workflow prototype. The project uses Razor pages/components
                for the user interface, C# for workflow logic, model classes for business records, local seeded data for demo review,
                and reporting pages that reuse the same operational and compliance records across multiple management views.
            </p>

            <ul class="action-list">
                <li>Razor pages for each major business module.</li>
                <li>Reusable visual patterns for cards, tables, badges, page intros, and workflow guidance.</li>
                <li>Business records grouped by owner, status, priority, due date, and module.</li>
                <li>Reporting, workload, reminders, data quality, and activity history built around shared workflow concepts.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Architecture Style</h2>
                    <p>The project is built like a modular internal business system.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="technical-highlight">
                <span>Architecture pattern</span>
                <strong>Module-based workflow app</strong>
                <p>
                    Each module has a clear business purpose, but the management pages combine records across modules.
                    That makes the project more useful than isolated CRUD pages because the same data supports safety review,
                    workload review, reminders, reporting, data quality, and portfolio explanation.
                </p>
            </div>

            <ol class="action-list">
                <li>Operational modules create and maintain records.</li>
                <li>Compliance modules surface review and follow-up pressure.</li>
                <li>Management modules group records for reporting and decision-making.</li>
                <li>System pages explain scope, value, rollout, review evidence, and production path.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="technical-card-grid">
        @foreach (var card in TechnicalCards)
        {
            <article class="technical-card">
                <div class="technical-card-header">
                    <span>@card.Number</span>
                    <div>
                        <p class="eyebrow">@card.Category</p>
                        <h2>@card.Title</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <p>@card.Description</p>

                <ul>
                    @foreach (var item in card.Items)
                    {
                        <li>@item</li>
                    }
                </ul>
            </article>
        }
    </section>

    <section class="report-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Module Architecture Map</h2>
                <p>How the main pages fit into the technical and workflow structure.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <table class="report-table technical-module-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Layer</th>
                    <th>Module / Page</th>
                    <th>Technical Role</th>
                    <th>Business Role</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var module in ModuleMap)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><span class="@module.BadgeClass">@module.Layer</span></td>
                        <td><strong>@module.Module</strong></td>
                        <td>@module.TechnicalRole</td>
                        <td>@module.BusinessRole</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Data Flow</h2>
                    <p>How information moves through the prototype.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="technical-flow-list">
                @foreach (var step in DataFlow)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@step.Number</span>
                        <div>
                            <strong>@step.Title</strong>
                            <p>@step.Description</p>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Technical Proof Points</h2>
                    <p>What this project demonstrates to a technical reviewer.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="technical-proof-grid">
                @foreach (var proof in ProofPoints)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@proof.Label</span>
                        <strong>@proof.Title</strong>
                        <p>@proof.Description</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Production Technical Upgrade Path</h2>
                <p>What would need to change before this became a live business system.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <table class="report-table technical-upgrade-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Area</th>
                    <th>Prototype State</th>
                    <th>Production Requirement</th>
                    <th>Recommended Upgrade</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var upgrade in UpgradeItems)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>@upgrade.Area</strong></td>
                        <td><span class="@upgrade.BadgeClass">@upgrade.PrototypeState</span></td>
                        <td>@upgrade.ProductionRequirement</td>
                        <td>@upgrade.RecommendedUpgrade</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="report-card technical-summary-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Technical Summary</h2>
                <p>A short technical description for portfolio review.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="technical-summary-copy">
            <p>
                OperationsFlow is a Blazor/.NET business workflow prototype that demonstrates modular page design,
                reusable UI patterns, workflow-oriented records, reporting views, activity traceability, and data quality review.
                The project uses realistic seeded data to show how operational records can feed management views such as workload,
                reminders, safety meeting summaries, compliance planning, reports, and system health checks.
            </p>

            <p>
                A production version would add authentication, role-based permissions, hosted SQL storage, Microsoft 365 integrations,
                document storage, API endpoints, automated tests, deployment pipeline, backups, logging, monitoring, and support documentation.
                The current version is intentionally scoped as a local portfolio prototype with clear production upgrade planning.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

